    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0148" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.79614/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-15T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                                1927—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your despatch 1415, February 4.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d61-f1"/> Article 24 of
                    the contract apparently grants a virtual monopoly of air traffic between the
                    points mentioned in Article 1. Please call this to the attention of the
                    appropriate authorities and express the hope of this Government that no
                    exclusive concession, preference or monopoly will be granted which would deny to
                    American citizens a fair and equal opportunity to compete in commercial aviation
                    in Guatemala.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="15" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted a copy of the proposed contract between Francisco
                    Buch de Parada and the Government of Guatemala.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
